From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: bringing a webview's page to the front fronts its
 window

At Chromium 160 `Page.bringToFront` activates only the outermost
WebContents. A <webview>'s page is an inner WebContents, and its own
delegate, WebViewGuest, is what asks the shell to front the window it is
in, so bringing that page to the front over DevTools no longer reached the
shell. Chromium 159 activated the page's own WebContents, and
guard-webview-activate presses with it.

- `PageHandler::BringToFront`: an inner WebContents is activated too,
  before the outermost one, and the handler stops if that destroyed it.
---
 content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc
index 5a2a450..df2de21 100644
--- a/content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc
+++ b/content/browser/devtools/protocol/page_handler.cc
@@ -1958,6 +1958,17 @@ Response PageHandler::BringToFront() {
   }
 
   base::WeakPtr<PageHandler> weak_self = weak_factory_.GetWeakPtr();
+  // Domicile's engine fork: a <webview>'s page is an inner WebContents, whose
+  // delegate fronts the window it is in. Activate it as well as the outermost
+  // one, as Chromium 159 did.
+  WebContentsImpl* web_contents =
+      WebContentsImpl::FromRenderFrameHostImpl(host_);
+  if (web_contents != web_contents->GetOutermostWebContents()) {
+    web_contents->Activate();
+    if (!weak_self || !host_) {
+      return Response::ServerError(kErrorNotAttached);
+    }
+  }
   WebContentsImpl::FromRenderFrameHostImpl(host_)
       ->GetOutermostWebContents()
       ->Activate();
